From: OCCTSwift ecosystem <noreply@secondmouse.au>
Subject: [PATCH] Modeling Algorithms - BRepOffsetAPI_MiddlePath::Build leaves the
 builder not done where a path stops short of the end section, instead of reading
 past it

BRepOffsetAPI_MiddlePath::Build starts one path per vertex of the start section and
marches each along the edges of the solid until it reaches a vertex of the end section.
It then builds one section per level by reading level i of two neighbouring paths. That
assumes every path reaches the end section, and for a pair of faces that are not the two
ends of a pipe it does not, and nothing checks:

  - Paths are padded to the current level with the last vertex of the previous edge, but
    only by one element, and the element read is cast with the unchecked TopoDS::Edge. A
    path that has already been padded once ends in a vertex, so the second pad casts a
    vertex, appends a null shape, and the next myPaths(k)(i).ShapeType() dereferences it.
    A path that stops short of the end section also never lets the "all end edges
    reached" exit fire, so the level loop has no other way to stop. Reads at lines 580
    and 584 of the V8_0_1 file, 91 of the 116 pairs measured.
  - A path that is a bare vertex at level i takes the edge at level i - 1 as E1 or E2
    with an unchecked cast. At level 1 there is no level 0, and elsewhere the element
    can be a vertex too. Lines 664 and 668, 21 pairs.
  - No face holds both the edge of a path and the edge of the section it is joined to,
    so theFace stays null and BRep_Tool::CurveOnSurface is called with it. Lines 672 and
    706, 4 pairs.

Each of the three is now checked and Build returns, leaving the builder not done, as it
already does when a start vertex has no edge outside the start wire.

Measured over 573 pairs of faces of 16 solids with Scripts/repro/3105-middlepath-patch,
one pair per process: the 116 pairs that share no vertex and are not the same face and
abort the process on the shipped kernel answer not done with the patch; the 42 pairs that
return a path return the same one (edge count, length and centre of mass agree to six
places); the 37 that throw and the 19 that answer not done are unchanged.

diff --git a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKOffset/BRepOffsetAPI/BRepOffsetAPI_MiddlePath.cxx b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKOffset/BRepOffsetAPI/BRepOffsetAPI_MiddlePath.cxx
index 5debda94..402ab2ed 100644
--- a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKOffset/BRepOffsetAPI/BRepOffsetAPI_MiddlePath.cxx
+++ b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKOffset/BRepOffsetAPI/BRepOffsetAPI_MiddlePath.cxx
@@ -110,6 +110,13 @@ static GeomAbs_CurveType TypeOfEdge(const TopoDS_Edge& anEdge)
   return BAcurve.GetType();
 }
 
+//! Returns true if the path holds an edge, and not a vertex, at the given level.
+static bool IsEdgeAt(const NCollection_Sequence<TopoDS_Shape>& thePath, const int theLevel)
+{
+  return theLevel >= 1 && theLevel <= thePath.Length()
+         && thePath(theLevel).ShapeType() == TopAbs_EDGE;
+}
+
 static gp_Vec TangentOfEdge(const TopoDS_Shape& aShape, const bool OnFirst)
 {
   TopoDS_Edge        anEdge = TopoDS::Edge(aShape);
@@ -547,12 +554,20 @@ void BRepOffsetAPI_MiddlePath::Build(const Message_ProgressRange& /*theRange*/)
       // for the end of initial shape
       if (myPaths(j - 1).Length() < i)
       {
+        if (!IsEdgeAt(myPaths(j - 1), i - 1))
+        {
+          return; // the path ended before the end section
+        }
         TopoDS_Edge  aE1     = TopoDS::Edge(myPaths(j - 1)(i - 1));
         TopoDS_Shape LastVer = TopExp::LastVertex(aE1, true);
         myPaths(j - 1).Append(LastVer);
       }
       if (myPaths((j <= NbPaths) ? j : 1).Length() < i)
       {
+        if (!IsEdgeAt(myPaths((j <= NbPaths) ? j : 1), i - 1))
+        {
+          return; // the path ended before the end section
+        }
         TopoDS_Edge  aE2     = TopoDS::Edge(myPaths((j <= NbPaths) ? j : 1)(i - 1));
         TopoDS_Shape LastVer = TopExp::LastVertex(aE2, true);
         myPaths((j <= NbPaths) ? j : 1).Append(LastVer);
@@ -615,6 +630,11 @@ void BRepOffsetAPI_MiddlePath::Build(const Message_ProgressRange& /*theRange*/)
         }
       }
 
+      if (theFace.IsNull()) // no face holds both the path edge and the section edge
+      {
+        return;
+      }
+
       TopoDS_Vertex PrevVertex =
         (E1.IsNull()) ? TopoDS::Vertex(myPaths(j - 1)(i)) : TopExp::LastVertex(E1, true);
       TopoDS_Vertex CurVertex = (E2.IsNull()) ? TopoDS::Vertex(myPaths((j <= NbPaths) ? j : 1)(i))
@@ -661,10 +681,18 @@ void BRepOffsetAPI_MiddlePath::Build(const Message_ProgressRange& /*theRange*/)
         {
           if (E1.IsNull())
           {
+            if (!IsEdgeAt(myPaths(j - 1), i - 1))
+            {
+              return;
+            }
             E1 = TopoDS::Edge(myPaths(j - 1)(i - 1));
           }
           if (E2.IsNull())
           {
+            if (!IsEdgeAt(myPaths((j <= NbPaths) ? j : 1), i - 1))
+            {
+              return;
+            }
             E2 = TopoDS::Edge(myPaths((j <= NbPaths) ? j : 1)(i - 1));
           }
           double                    fpar1, lpar1, fpar2, lpar2;
